      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T04:05:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The interop database is not generic across all form factors. See crrev/c/5084273, it only applies to the downstream system that chooses to specify it in the configure file.\n\nMy rationale to put system configuration prior to interop database is based on the original presentation of the code. i.e.,:\n1. There was a need for system-wide delay. \n2. There was NO need for a device-specific delay.\n\nBut rethinking this, I think system-wide property should be the baseline, and device-specific should be able to overwrite system-wide settings. So \"interop database to take priority over the property\"",
